{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And he anointed the Tabernacle, etc.</b> The reason Scripture interrupted between the dressing of Aaron and his anointing with the anointing of the Tabernacle and its vessels, is that we find that HaShem commanded the anointing of the Tabernacle and its vessels before the anointing of Aaron, as stated in parashat Pekudei (Exodus 40:9), and it would have been fitting to precede the anointing of the Tabernacle also before the dressing of Aaron in his garments, as stated there. And the reason he did not do so is that he examined closely the statement of HaShem here in this parashah (verse 2), where He said to him: ״קַח אֶת אַהֲרֹן וְגוֹ׳ וְאֵת שֶׁמֶן הַמִּשְׁחָה״ etc. — and if the anointing of the Tabernacle also preceded the dressing of Aaron in his garments, it should have said ״קַח אֶת שֶׁמֶן הַמִּשְׁחָה״, since that is the thing from which he would perform the first commandment, which is the anointing of the Tabernacle. And there is no room to err in his statement ״קַח אֶת שֶׁמֶן הַמִּשְׁחָה״ — that first he should anoint Aaron before dressing him in his garments — for after all He already said ״וְהִלְבַּשְׁתָּ אֶת אַהֲרֹן וְגוֹ׳ וּמָשַׁחְתָּ אוֹתוֹ״ (Exodus 28:41). Rather, it is certain that His intention is to precede the dressing of the garments before the anointing of the Tabernacle, and the fact that in parashat Pekudei He preceded the anointing of the Tabernacle to the dressing of Aaron's garments and to his anointing — that precedence applies only to his anointing specifically. But because Scripture did not wish to interrupt between the commandment of the garments and the commandment of Aaron's anointing, therefore it stated all the laws of Aaron together. And in any case the anointing of the Tabernacle and its vessels precedes only the anointing of Aaron and not the garments, as it revealed here, as mentioned."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:54:21.794715726Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}